<p>President Donald Trump said the United States should have a role in selecting Iran’s next leader, comments that several outlets said could sharpen questions about U.S. and Israeli war aims—and whether they point to regime change or are limited to altering Iranian behavior and policies. He also criticized the prospect of Ayatollah Ali Khamenei’s son, Mojtaba Khamenei, succeeding his father. The remarks add a fresh diplomatic flashpoint as the conflict is described as widening and reverberating across the region.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/QwsdwoFOsIEfYN7kTZdz7vXpRaz17obPUeN0DhFq1fauE_w_wHiB_fhMD8WczCDf-hFSGR0zeRQ4A1BtzVosz7xZTE7I4ZFil-ytPQMVL-Bk6LDhW2QPatjV6VZQ-lsWUDYj8ELb6-GMSGYXO52OKtQeKGic1_Y7BvFwS1EI9kIN4MtamOJ1a03Kvz19akcsPHP8aP0EqWsKkMzCBB-KA9wVjT1C2V5ntTo' alt='President Trump said Mojtaba Khamenei, a son of the former Iranian leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei who appeared to be the leading candidate to succeed his father, was an “unacceptable” choice.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Descriptors used: Coverage highlighted Trump’s blunt language about Mojtaba Khamenei—calling him “unacceptable” and a “lightweight”—as he dismissed him as a plausible successor.</li><li>Warning of future conflict: One account said Trump paired his succession comments with a warning of more war ahead if a preferable alternative leader did not emerge.</li><li>Wartime backdrop: Trump spoke as outlets described the Israel-Iran war as widening and rippling across the region, raising the diplomatic stakes of any U.S. talk about postwar leadership in Tehran.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>PBS NewsHour: It said Trump’s comments would likely revive questions about whether U.S. and Israeli goals are to topple Iran’s Islamic Republic or to press for narrower changes in Iranian policies. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/trump-says-he-wants-to-be-involved-in-picking-irans-next-leader'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>Semafor: It said Trump’s stance muddies Washington’s motives for the war by stretching the stated objectives toward choosing Iran’s leadership. (<a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/03/05/2026/trump-wants-to-help-pick-next-iran-leader'>Semafor</a>)</li><li>The New York Times: It framed Trump’s remarks as his most detailed yet on a U.S. role in shaping a new government in Tehran. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/05/us/politics/trump-iran-leader.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/us-iran-war-spreads-azerbaijan-israel-strikes-tehran-lebanon/'>Trump says he must have a role in choosing Iran&#x27;s next leader as war expands</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/trump-says-he-wants-to-be-involved-in-picking-irans-next-leader'>Trump says he wants to be involved in picking Iran&#x27;s next leader</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/05/us/politics/trump-iran-leader.html'>Trump Says He Should Have Role in Choosing Iran’s Next Leader</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/03/05/2026/trump-wants-to-help-pick-next-iran-leader'>Trump wants to help pick next Iran leader</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/khameneis-son-is-a-lightweight-trump-rejects-mojtaba-seeks-role-in-choosing-irans-next-leader-13986656.html'>&#x27;Khamenei’s son is a lightweight&#x27;: Trump rejects Mojtaba, seeks role in choosing Iran’s next leader</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/05/trump-insists-on-say-in-pick-of-next-iranian-supreme-leader_6751136_4.html'>Trump insists on say in pick of next Iranian supreme leader</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/trump-demands-say-on-irans-next-supreme-leader-as-israel-iran-war-ripples-across-the-region/article70709932.ece'>Trump demands say on Iran&#x27;s next supreme leader as Israel-Iran war ripples across West